  "query_preview": "..\n\nNext 7 days (through Thursday)...\n\nDense Fog Advisory has been issued through 11am for Carter/Fallon\ncounties for areas of upslope fog with visibilities of 1/4sm or \nlower. With temperatures near freezing be alert for slick icy\nspots on roadways, especially on bridges. Plan extra time to get\nto your destination safely this morning. Chambers\n\nSoutheast winds will increase throughout the day today east of\nRosebud County as a surface pressure gradient tightens and 850 mb\nwinds increase into the 30-40 kt range. 30-45 mph wind gusts are\nexpected with the strongest winds being near the Dakotas border.\nWinds will peak Friday afternoon and early evening before leveling\noff in the 30s mph Friday night and Saturday. Winds are expected\nto decrease Saturday evening. \n\nAbove average high temperatures in the 50s and 60s F and dry \nconditions are expected through Monday. There is increasing\nconfidence in a pattern change for the middle to late week period.\nThere is a 30-50% chance for getting greater than 0.25 inches of\nprecipitation. Temperatures are also expected to decrease to more\nseasonable values in the 40s F. Details such as precipitation \ntype and the potential locations of the heaviest precipitation \nare not known at this time. Torgerson",
